Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Back to Define Controls
Create a Control Which is Part of the Object
If you want all instances of a class to provide the same control, you typically create that control as a
user-defined attribute in the class.
To create a control as a user-defined attribute of data type method of the object:
• Type a meaningful name into the text box, right-click in the text box and select Create
Control. Plant Simulation then inserts self.Name_you_typed_in_for_the_control, such as
self.mySelectControl.
• Right-click in the text box and select Create Control on the context menu. Plant Simulation then inserts
self.OnBuilt_in_name_of_the_control, such as self.OnCreate.
Create a Control Which is Part of the Object
